From ab72685b2a4966204a781cdc94ff5054aea717fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 03:13:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 191/307] feat: nested LPV cascades (r_LPVCascades) - v2 item 2

Two nested volumes instead of a hard GI cutoff at the volume edge:
cascade 0 is the detail volume (r_LPVSize), cascade 1 covers
r_LPVCascadeScale (default 4) times the extent at the same grid
resolution.

- Both cascades inject from the single shared RSM; the only 3DEngine
  change is GetLPVBox() sizing the RSM box to the far cascade.
- All per-volume state moved into SCascade (textures, injection buffer,
  pass objects, origin/cell/accumulation/history); the relight chain
  runs per cascade with the cascade's own constants - every compute
  shader is shared unchanged, only the screen space apply reads both
  volumes and blends them over the near fade band (the far lookup uses
  its own half-cell normal offset).
- Relight gating shares the sun/heartbeat criteria, the origin-changed
  criterion is per cascade.
- Removed the dead screen space injection pass (unused since the bounce
  moved to the SVOGI style surface cache).

